question:
What is the key difference between display: flex and display: grid for laying out child elements?
```css
.flex-container { display: flex; }
.grid-container { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
```

Given this absolutely positioned element, what determines its containing block?
```css
.parent { position: relative; }
.child { position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; }
```

What is the most reliable modern method to clear floats and prevent layout collapse?
```css
.container::after { content: ''; display: table; clear: both; }
.float-item { float: left; }
```

How does position: relative differ from position: absolute in space consumption?
```css
.relative { position: relative; top: 50px; }
.absolute { position: absolute; top: 50px; }
```

What happens to horizontal centering when this CSS is applied?
```css
.box {
  position: absolute;
  left: 0;
  right: 0;
  margin: 0 auto;
}
```

Why might position: fixed behave unexpectedly inside a transformed parent?
```css
.parent { transform: scale(1); }
.fixed { position: fixed; }
```

In a flexbox container, what does display: table do to children?
```css
.flex-parent { display: flex; }
.table-child { display: table; }
```

When will position: sticky fail to stick to the viewport?
```css
.sticky { position: sticky; top: 0; }
.container { overflow: hidden; }
```
